I go to the shop on Sunday morning.
Now the shop is somewhat empty.
The same shopkeeper is there.
I go to him.
"Bhaiya, hello," I say.
"Hello madam, what do you need today?" he asks.
I take the shirt and the receipt out of the bag.
"Yesterday I bought this shirt here," I tell him.
"I also have its receipt."
He looks at the receipt and nods his head.
"What is the problem with the shirt?" he asks.
"This shirt is very small for me," I explain.
"Can I exchange this?" I ask.
"Yes madam, you can exchange it," he says.
"Please, give me a size bigger than this," I say.
"Do you have a shirt bigger than this one?"
"Yes, I will show you a bigger size," he says.
He places another shirt on the counter.
I look at that new shirt.
